{
  "requirement": "`Validation::execute` can compute an answer without a configured model provider.\nA validation that never invokes the agent interface does not fail because no\nagent is configured. Evidence storage is still required.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations derived from `requirements.sdk.graph.validation.deterministic_procedures`**\n1. `Validation::execute` can compute an answer with no model provider configured.\n2. A validation that never invokes the agent interface must not fail because no agent is configured.\n3. Evidence storage is still required.\n\n**Tests**\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_have_independent_typed_answers_and_cache_negative_results]`\n  - It builds `Validator::new(&domain)` and never calls `with_agent`.\n  - `Review::execute` (in `impl[Review<O>/Validation<Application>]`) never touches an agent.\n  - Several `verify` calls all succeed with `unwrap()`. They cover a typed answer, a `Vec<String>` and a `Judgment` with a negative result. Their outputs equal the expected values.\n  - Evidence storage is exercised and asserted:\n    - `state.executions == 3` and `state.writes == 3`.\n    - The stored record outputs for the `behavior` and `judgment` criteria equal the expected JSON.\n    - `check` returns `Current` for a stored criterion and `Missing` for a criterion with no record.\n  - This establishes obligations 1 and 2 (no `NoAgentConfigured` failure) and obligation 3 (answers are persisted).\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs#fn[runner_reuses_negative_judgments_and_records_only_callback_observations]`\n  - It uses a `Validator::new(&graph)` with no agent, and `Memory::run_review` makes no `ask` call by default.\n  - `verify` succeeds with `.unwrap()` and returns a result.\n  - A second `verify` reuses the stored evidence, so `state.started == [9]`.\n  - The record is stored with no dependencies.\n  - `check` returns `Current`, `Missing` or `Stale` as expected.\n  - A re-verify at revision `v2` rewrites the record.\n  - This shows the deterministic path works without an agent and that evidence storage is used.\n\n**Contrast case**\n- `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls` shows that a validation that does call the agent fails with `NoAgentConfigured` when none is configured.\n- That test is not marked for this requirement. The contrast is not needed here, and the deterministic path is already covered by the two tests above.\n\n**\"Evidence storage is still required\"**\n- This is a trait-level requirement. The validator is constructed from a graph that must provide the evidence storage, and the tests assert that evidence is written and read.\n- No separate failure scenario is stated for a missing store, so none is required.\n\n**Marking**\n- Both tests carry a `{test}` reference to the subject.\n\nI found no adequacy gaps.",
  "references": "5c244266cff9085a54f4213d7ebb031d46d2a78b63d9875ba1e4d3fb41c2acea",
